    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0475" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg427"/>

                <head>Mr. Thornton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 23, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit to you copy of
                    a dispatch addressed to Lord Stanley by Mr. Jorningham, her Majesty’s chargé
                    d’affaires <pb facs="0476" n="428" xml:id="pg428"/> at Lima, inclosing copy of a
                    letter addressed to him by the United States consul at Lambayeque, on the
                    subject of the ill treament of two British subjects by the revolutionary forces
                    in North Peru, and I have been instructed by his lordship to express to you the
                    thanks of her Majesty’s government for the friendly conduct of the United States
                    consul in this matter.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWARD THORNTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
